.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt XWEATHER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xweather
.Nd current weather in an X11 window
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dhqvV
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl display Ar name
.Op Fl H Ar host:port
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the current conditions for one place in a small window in the style of the Common Desktop Environment:
a picture for the conditions (sun, moon and stars, clouds, rain, snow, thunderstorm, fog), the temperature,
a description, wind and humidity, the time of the observation, and a status bar.
It uses the same settings file, built-in TLS library and data sources as
.Xr weather 1 .
.Pp
The window refreshes by itself every 15 minutes, which is how often the data source updates, unless that is
turned off.
If a refresh fails, the last good data stays on screen and the status bar says so and says how old the data is;
the next try comes after 1 minute and then waits twice as long each time, up to 15 minutes.
While a refresh is running the window stays alive, and closing it cancels the refresh at once.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file
Read and save settings in
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa ~/.weatherrc .
.It Fl d
Debug: log at the most detailed level and include the request and response text.
.It Fl display Ar name
The X display to use, as for any X program.
.It Fl h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl H Ar host:port
Testing only: plain HTTP to
.Ar host:port
instead of TLS to the data source.
.It Fl q
Log errors only.
.It Fl v
Log more.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh THE WINDOW
.Ss File menu
.Bl -tag -width "Location..." -compact
.It Sy Refresh
(F5) Fetch the weather now.
.It Sy Location...
(Ctrl+L) Open the Location dialog.
.It Sy Exit
(Ctrl+Q) Close the window.
.El
.Ss Options menu
.Bl -tag -width "Auto-refresh" -compact
.It Sy Auto-refresh
Turn the 15 minute refresh on or off.
.It Sy Imperial, Metric
Choose Fahrenheit and mph, or Celsius and km/h.
.El
.Ss Location dialog
Latitude, longitude and a name for the place, and a box for metric units.
Tab and Shift-Tab (or the arrow keys) move between the fields, Return accepts and Escape cancels.
A value that cannot be used is explained in red and nothing is saved.
Accepting saves the settings file and fetches the weather for the new place.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.weatherrc"
.It Pa ~/.weatherrc
Settings, see
.Xr weatherrc 5 .
Changes made in the window are written here.
.El
.Sh PLACE SEARCH
In Location, click Find or press Ctrl-F to search by name.
Search sends the explicit query to Open-Meteo geocoding over verified TLS;
opening the panel and typing send no requests.
Choose a result using the mouse or arrow keys, then Use to fill editable fields.
Location's OK saves separately; Cancel preserves the previous location.
The list credits Open-Meteo / GeoNames and shows country and coordinates.
Non-ASCII labels are simplified with an explicit note.
The free geocoding endpoint is for non-commercial use.
.Pp
Tab and Shift-Tab change focus; Ctrl-U clears the query.
Escape cancels a search, including while waiting for the network.
Ctrl-Q or closing the window cancels and quits.
Automatic weather refresh pauses while either Location panel is open.
A failed location save keeps the panel open and preserves the current forecast.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
The X display, unless
.Fl display
is given.
.El
.Sh X RESOURCES
.Nm
reads these from the X resource database
.Pq Xr xrdb 1
using the name
.Ql xweather .
.Bl -tag -width "xweather.background"
.It Ic xweather.background
The base colour; the light and dark bevel colours are derived from it.
Default is a blue-grey,
.Ql #AEB2C3 .
.It Ic xweather.foreground
Text colour.
.It Ic xweather.font
Normal font. The default is 12 point Helvetica, falling back to
.Ql fixed .
.It Ic xweather.boldFont
Bold font for the menu bar, buttons and headings.
.It Ic xweather.bigFont
Font for the temperature (24 point bold Helvetica by default).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after a normal exit.
Otherwise the values documented in
.Xr weather 1 ,
and 69 if the X display cannot be opened.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr weather 1 ,
.Xr weatherrc 5 ,
.Xr xrdb 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Jack Willis
